28
00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:51.620 line:15%
could be substituted as well.

29
00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.280
Good question.

30
00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.390
Oh, great question. Yeah, yeah. You can use chicken

31
00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.090
if you don't want to use any kind of seafood.

32
00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:01.580 line:15%
It really works with any protein. It's kind of up to you.

33
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.974 line:15%
Do you want- you ready to throw the pasta in?

34
00:01:03.974 --> 00:01:05.780 line:15%
I am!
This is a pretty quick-

35
00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.870
I am ready ready, Giada.

36
00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.000
I'm so-

37
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:10.833
ready.

38
00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:13.070
And I've got my pasta right here.

39
00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:14.100
Did you salt your water?

40
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.690
No, and I now know, I also learned, you know,

41
00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:23.690
what a cardinal no-no it is to put olive oil in the pasta.

42
00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:28.070
No olive oil in the pasta. You're ruining it.

43
00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:31.830
So once you get the salmon kind of cooking-

44
00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:32.663
Yep.

45
00:01:32.663 --> 00:01:34.550
you can add the red onion and the garlic.

46
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.600
Giada, I have a question.

47
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.433
Sure.

48
00:01:38.433 --> 00:01:40.080
If I did not have red onion,

49
00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.470
could I substitute a shallot or something else?

50
00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.480
Good question.

51
00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.940
Absolutely, you can definitely use shallots.

52
00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:50.280 line:15%
You can use a regular brown onion or white onion.

53
00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.350 line:15%
Really, any of it.

54
00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:54.150 line:15%
It's just to give it a little extra flair.

55
00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.670 line:15%
Yeah, it smells really good, and it's a really quick dinner.

56
00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.090
So once you've added the onion and the garlic,

57
00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:00.520
